  "ai_summary": "Consultancy stocks collapsed 26% this month (down 37% YoY), signaling investors expect AI to automate low-value outsourced work. OpenAI postings plummeted recently despite massive 696% annual growth, hinting at a hiring pullback. However, Indeed postings rose 2.6% (up 13.5% YoY), and Big Tech headcount remains stable (-2.2% monthly, -4.3% YoY). Devs aren't cooked, but the market is aggressively revaluing lower-skilled labor while maintaining core developer demand. Watching consultancy stocks collapse while dev demand holds steady is like seeing the iceberg sink instead of the Titanic.",
